{
	"ID": "20261101145217-38d4623",
	"Spec": "2",
	"Type": "NodeDocument",
	"Properties": {
		"id": "20261101145217-38d4623",
		"title": "Standalone Markdown editor",
		"type": "doc",
		"updated": "20261105091714"
	},
	"Children": [
		{
			"ID": "20261101145217-3a481f4",
			"Type": "NodeHeading",
			"HeadingLevel": 2,
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101145217-3a481f4",
				"updated": "20261105091714"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "Open and edit"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261101145217-925aeca",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101145217-925aeca",
				"updated": "20261103211019"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "On the Windows, macOS, and Linux desktop apps, launch SiYuan with "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "code",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "--markdown"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " to open an independent window. It works without opening a workspace or starting a local kernel. While this window is open, you can also start SiYuan normally to open the workspace interface."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261101153939-8444f00",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101153939-8444f00",
				"updated": "20261101153939"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "On Android, iOS, and HarmonyOS, choose SiYuan when a system file manager offers Open With for Markdown files to open the independent editor page. Document access comes from the system picker; some providers grant access only temporarily, so you may need to select the file again after restarting."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261101154840-193b541",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101154840-193b541",
				"updated": "20261105055849"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "The window title shows the current filename, or Untitled for a new document that has not been saved. Its header shows a file panel button, an outline button, the filename, Undo, Redo, and the "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "More"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " menu. There is no separate formatting toolbar. Desktop windows use an integrated title bar. File actions, editing modes, image insertion, resource authorization, recovery, theme, and font size are grouped there. The status bar shows additional actions only when needed. On desktop, toggle developer tools with "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "Ctrl+Shift+I"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " (Windows/Linux) or "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "Cmd+Alt+I"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " (macOS)."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261105055849-39489b5",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261105055849-39489b5",
				"updated": "20261105091714"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "Use the outline button next to the file panel button at the top left to show or hide the heading outline. The default shortcut is "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "Alt+2"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " on Windows/Linux and "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "Control+2"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " on macOS; check the button tooltip for any custom binding. It updates as you edit; expand or collapse nested headings and click a heading to jump to it. The outline is available in instant rendering and WYSIWYG modes when the window is at least 520 pixels wide. In source/split view or narrower windows, it is hidden and the button is disabled with an explanatory tooltip. Whether the outline is enabled is retained across documents only in the current window."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261102172700-0ood6fh",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261102172700-0ood6fh",
				"updated": "20261102172700"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "For ordinary Markdown resource links in a local workspace, choose "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "Open"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " - "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "Open in built-in Markdown editor"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " to edit the original resource file. This entry is unavailable for remote workspaces, encrypted notebook resources, and external file links, so remote paths and decrypted temporary copies are not mistaken for the original file."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261101145217-639d4db",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101145217-639d4db",
				"updated": "20261101145217"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "This editor opens ordinary UTF-8 .md and .markdown files. It does not import them into a notebook, convert them to .sy documents, or add them to workspace search, block references, or sync."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261101145217-918e675",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101145217-918e675",
				"updated": "20261101145217"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "After installing a desktop package with file association support, choose SiYuan from the system Open With menu. Installation adds a candidate without taking over your existing default application. You can also pass --markdown to the desktop executable for a blank document, or --markdown=\"path/to/file.md\" to open a file. In the editor, choose "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "More"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " - "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "Open"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " or drop a Markdown file. Opening a file already used by another editor window focuses that window."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261101145217-3d23d38",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101145217-3d23d38",
				"updated": "20261101171827"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "Use "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "More"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " - "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "Editing mode"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " to select instant rendering, WYSIWYG, or split view; a check mark identifies the current mode. Switching modes alone does not save the file. Editing may normalize Markdown formatting while retaining its content. Theme and font size are selected from the same style of checked submenus under "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "More"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " - "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "Appearance"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " and are stored independently of workspace settings."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261101171827-eb329f4",
			"Type": "NodeHeading",
			"HeadingLevel": 2,
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101171827-eb329f4",
				"updated": "20261105091714"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "Navigate Markdown files"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261101171827-c7e4443",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101171827-c7e4443",
				"updated": "20261102140506"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "Opening A.md uses its containing folder as the default file-tree root. The tree shows real folders and .md or .markdown files, loading each folder when expanded. Folders appear first, followed by filenames in natural order, so file2.md comes before file10.md. Folders expand and collapse with a smooth transition that respects the system’s reduced motion setting. Empty folders have no placeholder child row."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261101171827-4756559",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101171827-4756559",
				"updated": "20261105091714"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "Use the file panel button at the top left to show or hide the sidebar on desktop or the file drawer on mobile. The default shortcut is "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "Alt+1"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " on Windows/Linux and "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "Control+1"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " on macOS. When opened from a workspace, both panel shortcuts follow that workspace’s bindings; check the button tooltips for the current keys. Without a source workspace, the defaults apply. Both panels open and close with smooth transitions that respect the system’s reduced-motion setting. The filename toggles the panel only in the mobile or narrow-screen drawer layout; it is not clickable in the desktop sidebar layout. Drag the desktop sidebar divider to adjust its width. If a mobile provider grants access to only one file, select its containing folder when asked to enable the tree. Cancelling folder authorization leaves the current document editable. Tree access does not authorize local images."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261101171827-d330cb9",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101171827-d330cb9",
				"updated": "20261101171827"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "Click a file once to switch within the same editor container. The editor first checks the new file and protects the current document by saving or keeping a recovery draft; cancelling leaves the current document open. Switching inside the root keeps that root. Use "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "More"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " - "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "Open folder"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " to choose another navigation root without changing the document. Your chosen root stays selected even when the current document is outside it. Save As keeps the root when the new file is inside it and follows the new parent folder when it is outside."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261101171827-baf12f5",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101171827-baf12f5",
				"updated": "20261101171827"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "Expanded folders and the desktop panel width are remembered. Directory changes and returning focus refresh the tree. If a directory contains too many entries, choose a smaller folder. This panel is for navigation; it does not rename, delete, or reorganize files by dragging. On desktop, the menu also lets you reveal the current saved file in the system file manager."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261101145217-73f343e",
			"Type": "NodeHeading",
			"HeadingLevel": 2,
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101145217-73f343e",
				"updated": "20261103224054"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "Save and resolve conflicts"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261101145217-d4abb18",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101145217-d4abb18",
				"updated": "20261103224054"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "Changes to a writable file are saved automatically after you pause typing. Choose "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "More"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " - "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "Save"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " to request an immediate save; a new document must first be saved to a chosen location. The bottom status bar stays hidden during ordinary editing and saving; automatic saving continues normally. It appears only when conflicts, failures, recovery errors, or other problems need attention or action."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261101153939-3662f3d",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101153939-3662f3d",
				"updated": "20261101174206"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "On Android, Save As uses the system file picker to choose a location and filename. On iOS and HarmonyOS, choose a destination folder first, then enter the filename. The status bar remains hidden after a successful save. Cloud synchronization is managed by the corresponding cloud drive. When the app enters the background, it attempts to persist the latest committed input and save pending changes. If the system terminates the process, only content already persisted can be recovered. On iOS, Markdown scenes and the workspace share one app process; a process crash or termination affects both."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261101145217-58b95b6",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101145217-58b95b6",
				"updated": "20261101145217"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "When another application changes the file, a clean document can reload. If you have edited it or a save is pending, automatic writeback stops. Review the changes, then reload, explicitly confirm an overwrite, or use Save As. Permission loss, deletion, or an uncertain write result also stops writeback; use Retry or Save As when offered. Reload results never replace newer input."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261101145217-b5aceca",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101145217-b5aceca",
				"updated": "20261101145217"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "Save As reserves the chosen destination before writing and switches the session only after a confirmed save. A destination already used by another editor window cannot be overwritten directly. Saving in a different folder keeps relative resource links unchanged and does not copy resources; review the warning and move resources or adjust links as needed."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261101145217-340865b",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101145217-340865b",
				"updated": "20261101175356"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "Existing UTF-8 BOM and the selected newline convention are retained when saving. A file with mixed newlines may be normalized on the first actual edit. Opening, viewing, and switching modes do not rewrite the original file. Unsupported encodings and files larger than 8 MiB are rejected without modifying them."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261101145217-94c2a68",
			"Type": "NodeHeading",
			"HeadingLevel": 2,
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101145217-94c2a68",
				"updated": "20261103141758"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "Images and preview"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261101145217-4cb46a7",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101145217-4cb46a7",
				"updated": "20261101145217"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "To insert an image, save the Markdown document first, then choose "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "More"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " - "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "Insert image"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " to choose the source image and a new destination file. The editor copies the image and inserts a relative reference only after the copy is confirmed. It does not overwrite an existing image or support a destination on another drive. This action authorizes the selected image only, not its entire folder. On Android, select the source image, authorize the Markdown document’s parent folder if needed, and enter an unused filename in that folder. The inserted image receives its own preview authorization."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261101145217-02a0d08",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101145217-02a0d08",
				"updated": "20261101145217"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "Choose "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "More"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " - "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "Authorize resource folder"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " to select the local folder containing images referenced by relative paths. Only supported images within explicitly authorized folders are displayed. A missing or unauthorized image keeps its original Markdown reference and shows an unavailable-resource notice. Temporary preview addresses are never written into the document. Folder authorization belongs to the current editor session. On Android, select the Markdown document’s direct parent folder. Supported images in that folder and its subfolders can be displayed; parent-directory references containing .. are unavailable."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261101145217-84cf6d4",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101145217-84cf6d4",
				"updated": "20261103141758"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "HTTP and HTTPS images, including SVG badges, are displayed directly without folder authorization. Protocol-relative image URLs use HTTPS. Image loading does not change the Markdown links. Audio, video, embedded pages, scripts, and remote diagram services remain blocked. Ordinary HTTP, HTTPS, and email links open through the system only after you click them. Math uses local resources; dynamic diagram source is shown as code."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261101145217-881e5bd",
			"Type": "NodeHeading",
			"HeadingLevel": 2,
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101145217-881e5bd",
				"updated": "20261103213209"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "Local recovery and privacy"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261101145217-ccb4817",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101145217-ccb4817",
				"updated": "20261101162448"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "A new blank document that has never been edited closes without confirmation and does not create a recovery draft. Unsaved changes remain protected, including documents edited and then cleared, non-empty copies, and restored drafts. If these documents cannot be saved when you close the window or have no filename, you can keep a recoverable draft, choose Save As, or cancel. Open "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "More"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " - "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "Recover drafts"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " to inspect and restore records; restoration does not silently overwrite the original file."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261101145217-3530d93",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101145217-3530d93",
				"updated": "20261103213209"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "On mobile devices, drafts use home/.config/siyuan/markdown/recovery/, where home is the app’s existing home directory. Editing preferences and file tree state are stored in its parent directory. Recovery drafts are stored unencrypted on this device in the Markdown editor’s private directory, outside the workspace. They are not protected by encrypted notebooks and are not included in SiYuan sync. Desktop OS backups or other backup software may include this directory. Mobile apps exclude their private Markdown directory from system backup; the original files you select remain subject to their file provider’s own backup and synchronization behavior."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261101145217-945689a",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101145217-945689a",
				"updated": "20261103203708"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "Files up to 8 MiB of UTF-8 data can be opened and saved. Above 256 KiB, the editor automatically uses source editing with preview disabled; rich modes become available again after reducing the content below that threshold. Automatic fallback affects only the current document and does not change the preferred editing mode; only explicit mode selections are remembered. The file budget includes BOM and encoded newlines. Recovery content has a separate 16 MiB limit per draft, with 256 MiB and 1024 records in total. A recovery draft above the file limit remains available for copying or reducing, but cannot be written back until it fits. Reaching a limit reports a failure without deleting unrecovered drafts; they do not expire automatically."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261101154840-f2ab78f",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261101154840-f2ab78f",
				"updated": "20261101154840"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
